WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
The first film followed inherited variants across generations.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:09.880
How can data show that selection, rather than chance, shaped a population shift?

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.520
Return to the same teal and gold map, now tied to Gorongosa elephants.

4
00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:22.903
Teal marks tuskless females, and gold marks tusked females.

5
00:00:24.643 --> 00:00:27.223
Historical film and photographs give the prewar group.

6
00:00:28.743 --> 00:00:30.243
Later sightings give the survivors.

7
00:00:31.703 --> 00:00:34.783
The bars use the reported group sizes and percentages.

8
00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.313
The teal share is higher among survivors.

9
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:46.013
What changed? Did individual elephants lose tusks, or do the two groups contain

10
00:00:46.013 --> 00:00:48.633
different shares of elephants born with each trait?

11
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.340
Track two schematic animals between panels.

12
00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.240
A gold animal stays gold, and a teal animal stays teal.

13
00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.540
The survivor group contains more teal because tuskless females survived poaching

14
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.540
more often.

15
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:14.573
Ivory poaching was a selective pressure because it affected the variants

16
00:01:14.573 --> 00:01:18.273
differently. Tusked elephants were killed more often.

17
00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:24.453
The data support a change in the population's makeup, not a choice or transformation

18
00:01:24.453 --> 00:01:25.453
by elephants.

19
00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:30.367
A severe population crash can also change shares by chance.

20
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:36.487
Researchers modeled the crash with equal survival for tusked and tuskless females.

21
00:01:37.827 --> 00:01:42.427
The observed rise was far beyond what that chance model usually produced.

22
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:47.417
Daughters born later kept tusklessness above the prewar share.

23
00:01:48.597 --> 00:01:52.537
That pattern fits an inherited trait and a response to selection.

24
00:01:53.777 --> 00:01:58.737
It still does not identify the exact allele or prove what happened to every

25
00:01:58.737 --> 00:01:59.737
elephant.

26
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.607
Now widen the picture.

27
00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:07.287
Populations usually produce more young than their environments can support.

28
00:02:08.547 --> 00:02:11.347
A female blue crab carries an enormous egg mass.

29
00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:15.087
An elephant mother invests years in a calf.

30
00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:18.607
Most crab young die before reproducing.

31
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.940
These are endpoints on a range, not two rigid boxes.

32
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.880
One strategy makes many young with less investment in each.

33
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.000
The other makes fewer young with more care.

34
00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.960
Many species fall between them.

35
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.550
For selection, count offspring that survive and reproduce.

36
00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.150
Strength, effort, and need are not the score.

37
00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:48.210
The conditions decide whether an inherited variant changes reproductive success.

38
00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:54.973
When inherited variations affect reproductive success, populations change across

39
00:02:54.973 --> 00:03:01.153
generations. In Gorongosa, the trait pattern, selective pressure, survival

40
00:03:01.153 --> 00:03:03.913
difference, and daughters all support that rule together.

41
00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.193
Before-and-after data show a pattern.

42
00:03:08.473 --> 00:03:13.533
The selective pressure, survival estimate, chance comparison, and later daughters

43
00:03:13.533 --> 00:03:15.833
make the selection explanation stronger.

44
00:03:17.153 --> 00:03:20.593
Good evidence supports a claim while keeping its limits visible.

45
00:03:21.683 --> 00:03:25.263
Read the bars as population snapshots, not biographies.

46
00:03:26.603 --> 00:03:29.363
Read the filter as a comparison, not a promise.

47
00:03:30.703 --> 00:03:34.963
Then ask whether inherited differences changed who left the next generation.
